@database.locking

Purpose:
  Concurrency control mechanisms.

UseWhen:
  - concurrent access to same data
  - need to prevent race conditions
  - need serializability

AvoidWhen:
  - read-only workloads
  - low concurrency expected

Why:
  Prevents data corruption in concurrent environments.

Types:
  pessimistic:
      Lock before access.

  optimistic:
      Detect conflicts at commit.

  multiversion:
      Multiple versions for readers.

Related:
  @database.transaction
  @database.replication

Examples:
  @project.payment
  @project.order

State: +
